# Styling Base Rules

## Prefix and naming

- **Component prefixes (`@uls-prefix`)**: Component/root classes that come from ULX (e.g. `ulx-table`, `ulx-dataview`, `ulx-grid`) are generated via the configured `@uls-prefix` (currently `ulx-`, see `styles/foundation/overrides/base/prefix-vars.overrides.less`). **Do not hardcode new `uls-...` component/root classes** in templates; use the existing ULX components and their base classes instead.
- **Utility classes from `utill.less`**: Low-level utility classes (spacing, flex, width/height, colors, etc.) defined in `node_modules/uls_v2/src/styles/uls-styles/less/base/utill.less` (e.g. `flex`, `gap-4`, `text-13`, `fg-secondary`, `w-250`) are used **as-is** — they intentionally have no `ulx-` prefix. You may freely compose these existing utilities in templates, but **do not invent new utility names** there; add them in `utill.less` (or an overrides file) if truly needed.
- **New classes in app code**: When you must add a new semantic class in demos or overrides, prefer:
  - Reusing existing utilities from `utill.less`, or
  - Attaching a new class via ULX styles that follows the `@uls-prefix` pattern (component-level), not by introducing ad-hoc `uls-...` names in templates.

## Components vs raw markup

- **ULX components first**: Whenever there is a first‑class ULX component (button, icon, input, chip/tag, avatar, split button, etc.), **use the component instead of raw elements with classes.**
- Examples:
  - Use `UlxButton` instead of a bare `<button>` with button classes.
  - Use `UlxChip` (or the relevant tag/badge component) instead of a bare `<span>` with tag classes.
- Only fall back to raw HTML + utility classes when there is **no ULX component** that fits the use case.

## Autogenerated demo documentation

- **Do not create, edit, or delete** any files under `ulx/src/demo/ulx-ember/app/documentation/`. That tree is **autogenerated**; changes there will be overwritten.
- Update **source demos** (e.g. `ulx/src/demo/ulx-ember/app/components/Demo/`) or the project’s doc/snippet generation pipeline instead, per your team’s workflow.
